  "historical": {
    "title": "Why the metformin charge was higher in September",
    "body": "Completed charges are established by two paid pharmacy claims for metformin 500 mg tablets, quantity 60 for a 30-day supply. On August 18, 2026, Oak Street Pharmacy applied the preferred retail cost-share category and the member paid $8.00. On September 16, 2026, Lakeview Pharmacy applied the standard retail cost-share category and the member paid $27.00.\n\nThe pharmacy classifications support this difference: Oak Street Pharmacy was classified as preferred retail on August 18, while Lakeview Pharmacy was classified as standard retail on September 16. The selected plan policy states that, under the recorded conditions, a matched 30-day metformin 500 mg supply is $8 at preferred retail and $27 at standard retail.",
